    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34584": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Psychology",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Lecturer in Psychology Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Lecturer in Psychology Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Interested candidates must submit the following items for consideration: A Letter of Application that addresses the candidate’s qualifications. Curriculum Vitae A Teaching Statement or Philosophy. Evidence of Teaching Ability. Contact information (phone and email) for at least three references. Unofficial undergraduate and graduate transcripts. Posting Details Position Details Title Lecturer in Psychology Appointment Status Non-Tenure Track Department IU South Bend Psychology Location South Bend Position Summary The Department of Psychology at Indiana University South Bend is seeking to fill the position of Lecturer in Psychology. The candidate must be able and willing to teach Introductory Psychology and undergraduate courses related to methodology (e.g., research methods, statistics, non-experimental design, and APA style writing.) The area of specialization is open. The teaching load is the equivalent of 12 credit hours of undergraduate coursework each semester (fall and spring). Summer teaching is voluntary and compensated separately. Lecturers are expected to participate in service activities to the department, school, campus, or community, such as regularly attending and participating in faculty meetings and serving on relevant committees. This position does not carry expectations for a research program or publications. The Psychology Department at IU South Bend offers a BA degree. The departmental mission balances traditional and innovative approaches while merging technical skills with conceptual and critical understanding. We educate students about the power of psychology to inform and affect society. EEO /AA Statement : Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. Campus Safety and Security : The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online. You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu or by visiting IUPD . https://protect.iu.edu/police-safety/annual-reports/index.html Basic Qualifications Required Basic Qualifications: MA degree in Psychology by the time of appointment is required, with specialization area open. Willingness and availability to teach in-person format. Preferred Basic Qualifications: Experience with a variety of teaching methods and curricular perspectives. Demonstrated effective teaching and communication skills. Familiarity with commonly used analytical tools (e.g., SPSS , Excel, R, Qualtrics, NVivo, and/or similar platforms). Ability to teach courses such as developmental, industrial/organizational, introductory, data science, ABA , community psychology, or emerging areas. Ph.D. in Psychology Department Contact for Questions Kevin Ladd kladd@iu.edu Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Special Instructions Interested candidates must submit the following items for consideration: A Letter of Application that addresses the candidate’s qualifications. Curriculum Vitae A Teaching Statement or Philosophy. Evidence of Teaching Ability. Contact information (phone and email) for at least three references. Unofficial undergraduate and graduate transcripts. For Best Consideration Date 11/15/2026 Expected Start Date 08/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101624-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Evidence of Teaching Ability Statement of Teaching Philosophy List Of References Transcript Optional Documents Other Other 2 Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34506": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Spanish",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Assistant Professor of Spanish Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Assistant Professor of Spanish Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Interested candidates must submit the following items for consideration:· A letter of application that addresses the candidate’s qualifications · Curriculum vitae · A teaching statement (or philosophy) · Contact information (phone and email) for at least three references. · Unofficial undergraduate and graduate transcripts Posting Details Position Details Title Assistant Professor of Spanish Appointment Status Tenure Track Department IU South Bend World Languages Location South Bend Position Summary The Department of World Language Studies at Indiana University South Bend is currently seeking qualified applicants for a full-time tenure track Assistant Professor in Spanish with a specialization in Latin American Literature or Spanish Applied Linguistics, beginning August 1, 2027. The successful candidate will contribute to our academic mission through teaching, scholarship, and service. The full-time load (100% FTE ) is 12 credit hours (typically four courses) each fall and spring semester, with one course reassigned time for scholarly and creative activities following university & campus policies. The successful candidate will teach three courses per semester, contribute to service, and have an active scholarship program. Faculty may be required to teach online and nonstandard hours. U.S. citizenship or lawful permanent residence status is required for tenure. Review of applications will begin on November 1st. The search will remain open until the position is filled. EO/AA Statement: Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University Notice of Non-Discrimination, which includes contact information. Campus Safety and Security: The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online. You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu or by visiting IUPD , https://protect.iu.edu/police-safety/annual-reports/index.html Basic Qualifications Required: • Ph.D. in Spanish or equivalent; ABD candidates will be considered if a Ph.D. will be in hand by the time of appointment. • Native or near-native proficiency in Spanish and English. • Evidence of innovative and effective Spanish language teaching. • Evidence of an active research agenda in the field of specialization. Preferred: •Spanish for Heritage Speakers. • Experience and / or interest in High-Impact educational practices such as Internships, Study Abroad and Community-engaged Teaching and Learning. • Demonstrated experience in mentoring students, including guiding involvement in extracurricular activities, such as the advising of student clubs. Department Contact for Questions Julio F Hernando Email: julherna@iu.edu Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank $55,000-$59,000 (FT3) Special Instructions Interested candidates must submit the following items for consideration:· A letter of application that addresses the candidate’s qualifications · Curriculum vitae · A teaching statement (or philosophy) · Contact information (phone and email) for at least three references. · Unofficial undergraduate and graduate transcripts For Best Consideration Date 11/01/2026 Expected Start Date 08/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101687-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Statement of Teaching Philosophy List Of References Transcript Optional Documents Other Other 2 Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34411": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor of Nursing",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Clinical Assistant Professor of Nursing Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Clinical Assistant Professor of Nursing Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please include Resume/CV Three professional references required Posting Details Position Details Title Clinical Assistant Professor of Nursing Appointment Status Non-Tenure Track Department IU South Bend Nursing Location South Bend Position Summary The Division of Nursing Science at Indiana University South Bend, within the Vera Z. Dwyer School of Health Sciences, invites applications for a full-time, ten-month, clinical (non-tenure track) faculty position beginning January 1, 2027. The Division of Nursing Science offers a traditional BSN program, a mobility-option RN-to- BSN program, and four MSN tracks (Family Nurse Practitioner ( FNP ), Post-Master’s FNP Certificate, Nurse Education, and Nursing Administration). The primary focus of this position is teaching MSN core courses, Family Nurse Practitioner clinical rotations, and Advanced Health Assessment lab. Additional teaching responsibilities may include laboratory, clinical, and lecture courses in the BSN program in the candidate’s areas of expertise. Preference will be given to those who have obstetrics or pediatrics experience. A typical full-time nursing faculty teaching assignment requires in-person teaching (lecture and clinical), class/ clinical preparation, grading, providing academic support to students, and engaging in service to the school, college, university, and community. Additional responsibilities include assistance with clinical simulation and may include development of new courses and/or development of new degree programs. Preference will be given to candidates who have the skills to teach across the MSN curriculum and the BSN program. The MSN Certification pass rates are consistently 100%, and graduates of the BSN and MSN programs are known for the quality of their academic and experiential preparation. The programs within the Division of Nursing Science are fully accredited by the Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education ( CCNE ). Basic Qualifications Required: An earned master’s degree in nursing is required, The candidate must have or be eligible to hold a current RN license in Indiana and have national certification as a Family Nurse Practitioner. A minimum of five years of previous clinical experience in a nursing role is required. Successful candidates will demonstrate excellence in teaching, communication, collaboration, professionalism, organizational skills, and emotional intelligence, including the ability to build positive relationships, communicate with empathy, and navigate challenging situations with integrity and respect. Preferred: A doctorate (PhD or DNP ) in nursing is preferred. Three or more years as a family nurse practitioner preferred. Previous clinical and/or academic lecture teaching experience is highly desired. Department Contact for Questions Andrea Borders Email: anbord@iu.edu Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank $70,000-$75,000 (FCX) Special Instructions Please include Resume/CV Three professional references required For Best Consideration Date 11/01/2026 Expected Start Date 01/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101683-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae List Of References Optional Documents Other Other 2 Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34405": {
      "title": "Subject &amp; Instruction Librarian (Part-time)",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Subject &amp; Instruction Librarian (Part-time) Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Subject & Instruction Librarian (Part-time) Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Details Title Subject & Instruction Librarian (Part-time) Appointment Status Non-Tenure Track Department IU South Bend Library Location South Bend Position Summary The IU South Bend Libraries seeks a part‑time, hourly librarian position (38 weeks during the academic year) reporting to the Director of Research and Learning. The successful candidate will support the university’s teaching, learning, and research mission through information literacy instruction, subject liaison responsibilities, and reference services. Primary responsibilities include teaching credit‑bearing information literacy courses, providing course‑integrated instruction, serving as subject librarian for selected academic programs, and providing reference services. The position also involves participation in library meetings, collaboration on projects and events, and contribution to a responsive and student‑centered library environment. Basic Qualifications Required Basic Qualifications: MLS from an ALA accredited program (American Library Association) required. Demonstrated experience in reference and instruction, preferably in an academic or specialized library required. Preferred Basic Qualifications: Teaching experience in an academic setting. Department Contact for Questions Vincci Kwong vkwong@iu.edu Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Special Instructions For Best Consideration Date 05/26/2026 Expected Start Date 08/10/2026 Posting Number IU-101558-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Letter of Application Other Other 2 Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
