    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34320": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Computer Science",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Assistant Professor in Computer Science Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Assistant Professor in Computer Science Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Interested candidates must submit the following items for consideration: · A letter of application that addresses the candidate's qualifications that includes a list of IU South Bend computer courses that you are able to teach · A curriculum vitae · A research statement including future plans · A teaching statement (or philosophy) · Contact information (phone and email) for at least three references · Unofficial undergraduate and graduate transcripts Posting Details Position Details Title Assistant Professor in Computer Science Appointment Status Tenure Track Department IU South Bend Computer Science Location South Bend Position Summary The Department of Computer and Information Sciences at Indiana University South Bend welcomes applications for a full-time Tenure-Track Assistant Professor position beginning August 1, 2027. We seek candidates who have earned, or are nearing completion of, a PhD in Computer Science or a closely related field, with research interests, experience, and demonstrated contributions in Artificial Intelligence. The successful candidate will contribute to our academic mission through teaching, scholarship, and service. The full-time load (100% FTE ) is 12 credit hours (typically four courses) each fall and spring semester, with one course reassigned time for scholarly and creative activities following university & campus policies. The successful candidate will teach three courses per semester, contribute to service, and have an active scholarship program. Faculty may be required to teach online and nonstandard hours. Salary and benefits are competitive. About the Department: The Department of Computer and Information Sciences at Indiana University South Bend offers undergraduate and/or graduate majors in Computer Science, Informatics, New Media, Data Science, and related fields. The department emphasizes high-quality teaching, active faculty scholarship, and strong connections to regional industry through internships, applied projects, and community engagement. The department is committed to preparing students for successful careers while fostering an enjoyable and collaborative workplace for faculty. About Indiana University: South Bend Indiana University South Bend is a public, comprehensive and the largest regional campus of Indiana University, serving northern Indiana and southwest Michigan. Located along the St. Joseph River, the campus is known for its strong emphasis on teaching excellence, undergraduate research, faculty student interaction, commitment to access and community engagement within a supportive academic environment. EO/AA Statement: Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. Campus Safety and Security: The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online. You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu or by visiting IUPD . https://protect.iu.edu/police-safety/annual-reports/index.html Basic Qualifications Required: Ph.D. in Computer Science or related field by August 1, 2027. Teaching experience in computer science. Effective oral and written communication skills. Preferred: Ph.D. in Computer Science with AI research experience. Ability to teach core computer science courses at multiple levels. Ability to teach online classes Department Contact for Questions Name: Dana Vrajitoru Email: dvrajito@iu.edu Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank $80,000-$90,000 (FTT) Special Instructions Interested candidates must submit the following items for consideration: · A letter of application that addresses the candidate’s qualifications that includes a list of IU South Bend computer courses that you are able to teach · A curriculum vitae · A research statement including future plans · A teaching statement (or philosophy) · Contact information (phone and email) for at least three references · Unofficial undergraduate and graduate transcripts For Best Consideration Date 01/01/2027 Expected Start Date 08/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101668-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research and Teaching List Of References Transcript Optional Documents Other Other 2 Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34318": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Fine Arts",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Assistant Professor of Fine Arts Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Assistant Professor of Fine Arts Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Interested candidates must submit the following items for consideration: -A letter of application that addresses the candidate’s qualifications · Curriculum vitae -An art statement and a teaching statement (or philosophy). -A PDF portfolio or link to a website of 20 images of personal work and student work -Contact information (phone and email) for at least three references. -Unofficial undergraduate and graduate transcripts Posting Details Position Details Title Assistant Professor of Fine Arts Appointment Status Tenure Track Department IU South Bend Fine Arts Location South Bend Position Summary The Fine Arts Department at Indiana University South Bend invites applications for Tenure-Track faculty in printmaking. The applicant should be an artist-scholar specializing in printmaking. The candidate should understand aesthetics, visual literacy, the history of art, and contemporary issues in art as related to printmaking and fine art practices. Each semester, the candidate will teach two printmaking classes and one course in the department’s general education curriculum. The full-time load (100% FTE ) is 12 credit hours (typically four courses) each fall and spring semester, with one course reassigned time for scholarly and creative activities following university & campus policies. The successful candidate will teach three courses per semester, contribute to service, engage in scholarly/creative activities, mentor students, and use their expertise to teach fine art students, particularly those students with a concentration or minor in printmaking. The faculty member will also manage and maintain the printmaking studio. This position begins on August 1, 2027. The candidate will have the opportunity to apply for tenure in their 6th year of service. IU South Bend is the third largest campus in the Indiana University system and serves the north central Indiana community. The growing Fine Arts Department at IU South Bend currently includes B.A. and B.F.A. degrees in studio arts and art education. The mission of the Fine Arts Department is to balance traditional and innovative approaches while merging technical skills with conceptual and critical understanding. We educate students about the power of visual arts to inform and affect society. EO/AA Statement : Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. Campus Safety and Security : The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online. You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu or by visiting IUPD . https://protect.iu.edu/police-safety/annual-reports/index.html Basic Qualifications Required: An MFA in printmaking or related studio art by time of appointment. Knowledge and ability to teach a variety of printmaking techniques that include but is not limited to relief, silkscreen, and etching. Effective oral and written communication skills. Preferred: Demonstrated potential for excellence in the areas teacher or studio practice. Experience in teaching as the faculty of record. Experience studio lab management. Ability to coordinate multiple sections and teach independent study students. Evidence of a strong commitment to ongoing professional development and creative studio practice. Demonstrated experience in mentoring students, including guiding involvement in extracurricular activities (e.g., advising of student clubs). Department Contact for Questions Susan Moore sulmoore@iu.edu Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank $55,000-$59,000 (FTT) Special Instructions Interested candidates must submit the following items for consideration: -A letter of application that addresses the candidate’s qualifications · Curriculum vitae -An art statement and a teaching statement (or philosophy). -A PDF portfolio or link to a website of 20 images of personal work and student work -Contact information (phone and email) for at least three references. -Unofficial undergraduate and graduate transcripts For Best Consideration Date 11/16/2026 Expected Start Date 08/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101655-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Statement of Teaching Philosophy List Of References Transcript Optional Documents Other Other 2 Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/33899": {
      "title": "Visiting Lecturer in Theatre",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Visiting Lecturer in Theatre Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Visiting Lecturer in Theatre Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Letter of Interest Teaching Statement that includes pedagogical philosophy and how it relates to your classroom teaching and co-curricular technical work. Unofficial Transcripts Curriculum Vitae Names and contact information for three references that can speak to your teaching and professional experience. Digital portfolio of representative work and/or a link to your website where examples of work are present. Posting Details Position Details Title Visiting Lecturer in Theatre Appointment Status Non-Tenure Track Department IU South Bend Theatre & Dance Location South Bend Position Summary The Theatre and Dance Department of Indiana University South Bend is seeking a Visiting Lecturer in Theatre, Technical Design to begin August 15, 2026. The Department, housed in the vibrant Ernestine M. Raclin School of the Arts a part of the College of Arts and Sciences, is a professionally engaged community of theatre makers with the goal of helping each of our students find and evolve their most trained, flexible, creative, and unique artist within while preparing them for further study in graduate school and/or work in the professional theatre world. The Department offers a BA in Theatre and BFA programs in Musical Theatre Performance and Design & Technical Production. The Theatre and Dance Department produces 2-4 productions per academic year including our children’s theatre series, which has been a beloved tradition in the region for nearly 60 years. The Visiting Lecturer is responsible for teaching and serving as the Technical Director/Scene Shop Supervisor. Courses will be within their specialty as well as general theatre courses. Possible courses include: Introduction to Theatre, Stagecraft, and Practicum as well as others determined by need and knowledge base. Technical Director responsibilities include mentoring students, building scenery, etc., as a part of our co-curricular production season. The Technical Director will oversee the operation and maintenance of the scenic construction and storage facilities including maintaining the operating budget for the scene shop and student labor. EEO /AA Statement : Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. Campus Safety and Security : The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online. You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu or by visiting IUPD . https://protect.iu.edu/police-safety/annual-reports/index.html Basic Qualifications Required Basic Qualifications: Masters degree or higher, or equivalent work experience. Theatre in Design and/or Technical Production; or related field (masters or above) with experience in theatre. Excellent communication skills. Budgeting and time management skills. General computer skills and proficiency in Vectorworks. Professional production experience. Preferred Basic Qualifications: MFA in Theatre in Design and/or Technical Production; or related field (masters or above) with experience in theatre. Experience teaching at the University level. Additional related skillsets (stage management, production management, etc.). Department Contact for Questions Jason Resler reslerj@iu.edu Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Special Instructions Letter of Interest Teaching Statement that includes pedagogical philosophy and how it relates to your classroom teaching and co-curricular technical work. Unofficial Transcripts Curriculum Vitae Names and contact information for three references that can speak to your teaching and professional experience. Digital portfolio of representative work and/or a link to your website where examples of work are present. For Best Consideration Date 08/01/2026 Expected Start Date 08/15/2026 Posting Number IU-101614-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Evidence of Teaching Ability Statement of Teaching Philosophy List Of References Transcript Optional Documents Other Other 2 Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/33898": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of English",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Assistant Professor of English Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Assistant Professor of English Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Interested candidates should send transcripts, curriculum vitae, and letter of application addressing research interests and teaching experience and philosophy. Posting Details Position Details Title Assistant Professor of English Appointment Status Tenure Track Department IU South Bend English Location South Bend Position Summary The English Department at Indiana University South Bend invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Composition and First Year Writing in the department’s expository writing program, to begin August 1, 2027. Applicants should have enthusiasm for teaching first-year students and First-Year Writing in a First Year Writing General Education program integrated within a collegial and lively English Department. The full-time load (100% FTE ) is 12 credit hours (typically four courses) each fall and spring semester, with one course reassigned time for scholarly and creative activities following university & campus policies. Successful applicants will be expected to demonstrate a commitment to quality instruction, maintain an active research agenda, and engage in service activities. EEO /AA Statement : Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. Campus Safety and Security : The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online. You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu or by visiting IUPD . https://protect.iu.edu/police-safety/annual-reports/index.html Basic Qualifications Required Basic Qualifications: PhD in Composition or First Year Writing; ABD candidates nearing completion of degree will be considered. Demonstrated excellence in teaching. Investment in a research agenda in the field. Active engagement in service activities. Commitment to supporting students from a wide range of educational backgrounds. Preferred Basic Qualifications: Experience or expertise in writing program leadership. Experience in curriculum development and program development. Strategies for student retention. Demonstrated scholarly activity in the field. Additional qualifications in Professional Writing or English as a Second Language a plus. Department Contact for Questions Elaine Roth elaroth@iu.edu Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Special Instructions Interested candidates should send transcripts, curriculum vitae, and letter of application addressing research interests and teaching experience and philosophy. For Best Consideration Date 11/02/2026 Expected Start Date 08/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101612-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcript Optional Documents Other Other 2 Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
